  "lineage": "Afro-Peruvian folk-popular dance-and-song tradition of coastal Peru (Lima, Chincha, El Carmen, Ica regions), descended from West-African-enslaved-population cultural memory through colonial-Peruvian slavery period. Fast 6/8 meter, virtuoso cajón lead, quijada jawbone-rattle, acoustic-guitar. Nicomedes Santa Cruz (1925-1992) and Victoria Santa Cruz (1922-2014) consolidated twentieth-century cultural revival. Susana Baca, Eva Ayllón anchor contemporary scene.",
